---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import refs from '../../../../../public/equipment/07-08/references.json';
import v from '../../../../../public/equipment/07-08/verification.json';
const a='/equipment/07-08/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Miltenyi gentleMACS Octo · Documentary exhibit" subtitle="" description="Orbit the closed legacy Octo exterior and use a separate static geometry plaque." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment oc0708">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/07-08/">← Equipment 07-08</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#evidence">Sources &amp; checks</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">07-08 / Documentary exterior and detached shapes</span><h2>Miltenyi gentleMACS Octo · Closed exterior &amp; shape plaque</h2><p>Inspect the legacy yellow-orange cabinet. On the separate geometry plaque, compare a square, octagon or disk with the same 24 mm outer radius. The shape drawing is unrelated to the instrument.</p></header>
<div class="dn-grid"><section class="dn-card"><h3>3D exhibit</h3>
<div class="dn-bar"><button data-view="whole">Whole exhibit</button><button data-view="front">Sloped fascia</button><button data-view="side">Case side</button><button data-view="chart">Shape plaque</button><button id="camera-reset">Reset view</button></div>
<div class="dn-camera"><canvas id="octo-model" aria-label="Dormant yellow and orange Octo cabinet and a separate geometry plaque"></canvas></div>
<p id="asset" class="dn-note" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="dn-note">Drag to orbit, pinch or scroll to zoom. On the separate plaque, the amber key cycles the shape and the pale key toggles the reference circle. The blank fascia and opaque top covers are fixed.</p></section>
<section class="dn-card"><h3>Compare static shapes</h3><div class="dn-bar"><label>Shape <select id="shape"><option value="octagon">Regular octagon</option><option value="square">Square</option><option value="disk">Disk</option></select></label><button class="primary" id="overlay" aria-pressed="true">Hide reference circle</button><button id="reset">Reset</button></div>
<canvas id="shape-chart" width="480" height="336" role="img" aria-label="Static polygon or disk with optional 48 millimetre diameter reference circle"></canvas>
<p class="dn-note" id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Regular octagon · area 1629.17 mm² · 90.03% of reference disk.</p>
<div class="dn-bar"><button id="json">Export comparison JSON</button><a href={a+'example-shape.json'}>Example reading</a></div>
<p class="dn-note">The reference disk has a 48 mm diameter. Polygon area uses the vertices' signed cross-sum; perimeter is the sum of edge lengths. Hiding the outline changes the picture, not the calculated area.</p></section></div>
<section id="evidence"><h3>Sources and geometric verification</h3>
<div class="photo-pair">
<figure><img src={a+'reference-overview.webp'} width="640" height="400" alt="Original front three-quarter render of the orange enclosure and sloping yellow panel" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Original front three-quarter render. The <a href={refs.references[0].url}>OEM manual cover</a> establishes the broad orange center and yellow sloped fascia. Its device accessories are not included in this reconstruction.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={a+'reference-side.webp'} width="640" height="400" alt="Original rear-side render showing sealed enclosure form and opaque caps" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Original rear-side render of the same GLB. Side proportions and fixed stylized caps are inferred, not parts drawings.</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<ul>{refs.references.map(r=><li><a href={r.url}>{r.title}</a>. {r.caption}</li>)}</ul>
<p>The authored legacy cabinet uses <b>285 × 465 × 185 mm</b> (W × D × H), from Miltenyi IM0008540 p. 81. This distinguishes 130-096-427 from the newer housing. The blank screen, closed silhouettes, and accessory omissions make this a passive exterior reference. No loading, material handling, dissociation, biological inputs/outputs, settings, or operating behavior are implemented; the register’s planned replay is not part of this page.</p>
<div class="dn-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{v.checks.map(c=><tr><th scope="row">{c.id}</th><td>{String(c.expected)} {c.unit}</td><td>{typeof c.actual==='number'?Number(c.actual.toFixed(8)):String(c.actual)} {c.unit}</td><td>{c.tolerance===0?'Exact':c.tolerance}</td><td>{c.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'build-model.py'} download>Editable model</a> · <a href={a+'octo-documentary.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'references.json'}>Reference notes</a> · <a href={a+'vr-station.json'}>VR action manifest</a> · <a href={a+'shapes.mjs'}>Geometry module</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification JSON</a>. No headset session tested.</p>
</section></article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/07-08/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
.oc0708{--dn-rule:color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 26%,transparent);max-width:1280px;margin:auto}.dn-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.08fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}.dn-card{min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--dn-rule);padding:.85rem;margin:.8rem 0}.dn-card h3{margin:.21rem 0 .6rem}.dn-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem;margin:.53rem 0}.dn-bar,.dn-note,.dn-fig figcaption{font:.89rem/1.4 system-ui,sans-serif}
.oc0708 :is(button,select){font:inherit;padding:.4rem;background:var(--panel,Canvas);color:inherit;border:1px solid var(--dn-rule);border-radius:3px;min-height:38px;cursor:pointer}.oc0708 .primary{background:#34594f;color:#fff}.dn-camera{aspect-ratio:1.34;background:#263b40}.dn-camera canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}.oc0708 #shape-chart{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:492px;margin:.6rem 0}.dn-table{overflow:auto}.dn-table table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}.dn-table :is(td,th){border-bottom:1px solid var(--dn-rule);padding:.42rem;text-align:left}.dn-fig{margin:1rem 0;max-width:680px}.dn-fig img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.dn-fig figcaption{margin:.38rem 0}@media(max-width:850px){.dn-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
.oc0708 .photo-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.8rem;max-width:860px}.oc0708 .photo-pair figure{margin:0}.oc0708 .photo-pair img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.oc0708 .photo-pair figcaption{font:.86rem/1.4 system-ui,sans-serif;margin:.3rem 0}@media(max-width:600px){.oc0708 .photo-pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
